summary: Cause a hardware device to violate the IOMMU by accessing an invalid, read-only, or unmapped page.
description: |
  This test causes a hardware device to attempt to access an invalid, read-only, or 
  unmapped page of the address space and confirms that this results in a graceful 
  failure. The test cases are designed to be part of the standard RHIVOS QE test 
  suite. QEMU is utilized to customize the devices, and the validation is performed 
  within the VM.
contact: Charles Shi <cheshi@redhat.com>
test: bash ./runtest.sh
framework: beakerlib
require:
  - ninja-build
  - gcc
  - make
  - libslirp
  - libslirp-devel
  - libguestfs
  - edk2-aarch64
  - screen
duration: 50m
id: 3271c39f-ec5e-4ec4-8b3d-ef0b8d2d3054
